+### Are the downstream metrics still moving?
+
+Prediction loss is not what the conclusions rest on, so we re-measured the downstream quantities at the saved epoch-10/20/30/40/50 checkpoints of 6 Dubins models (`epoch_downstream.py`, results `epoch_downstream.results.txt`). Per checkpoint: the GP margin function (5000 steps, red uniform states, seed-0 states) and its zero-shot AUC on color (mean ± std over 3 margin-function seeds), rotate and shape (seed 0); the same seed-0 margin function on imagined latents of 600 CEM-style plans (as Table 16); and goal-distance fidelity near the goal (Spearman between latent distance to the goal frame and true $(x, y)$ distance, true distance < 0.5, 400 held-out windows × 25 steps), on real and on imagined latents. The epoch-50 rows reproduce Table 16 (e.g. sigreg 0.814 / 0.423, jac+pull 0.961 / 0.281). Caveat: an epoch-30 checkpoint is not a model trained for 30 epochs, since the learning rate is still about 35% of its peak there.
